 "answer_html": "<h3>Definition</h3><p><b>Java 2D</b> lets us draw shapes using the <b>Graphics2D</b> class and shape classes from <code>java.awt.geom</code>, like <b>Line2D</b>, <b>Rectangle2D</b> and <b>Ellipse2D</b>.</p><h3>Key points</h3><ul><li>Cast <code>Graphics</code> to <b>Graphics2D</b>.</li><li>Create a shape object, e.g. <code>new Rectangle2D.Double(x, y, w, h)</code>.</li><li>Use <b>draw(shape)</b> for outline and <b>fill(shape)</b> to fill it.</li><li>Shape classes have <b>.Double</b> and <b>.Float</b> versions.</li></ul><table><tr><th>Shape class</th><th>Made with</th></tr><tr><td>Line2D</td><td>(x1, y1, x2, y2)</td></tr><tr><td>Rectangle2D</td><td>(x, y, width, height)</td></tr><tr><td>Ellipse2D</td><td>bounding box (x, y, width, height)</td></tr></table>",
 "quiz": {
  "q": "Which method fills the inside of a shape?",
  "options": [
   "g2.draw()",
   "g2.fill()",
   "g2.paint()"
  ],
  "answer": 1,
  "why": "draw = outline, fill = inside."
 }
